    <description>Fires when AF_DiscountApprovalStatus__c changes to Rejected. Notifies the Quote Owner via email and Custom Notification - same dual-channel pattern as AF_FL_Reservation_Rejected. logEmailOnSend+relatedRecordId=$Record.Id added so the email logs as an EmailMessage on the Quote&apos;s own Emails/Activity related list (previously sent but not logged anywhere). 2026-09-09: upgraded from plain text to branded HTML (sendRichBody=true). Tried real EmailTemplate + AF_SendTemplateEmailAction (Apex wrapper around Messaging.sendEmail(templateId=...)) first, since Flow&apos;s own &quot;emailTemplate&quot; core action is confirmed NOT a valid InvocableActionType in this org&apos;s Metadata API - but Messaging.sendEmail to a User target hard-requires saveAsActivity=false, and with that forced false, ZERO EmailMessage row is created (confirmed empirically: isSuccess()=true, no EmailMessage ever appears), unlike emailSimple+logEmailOnSend which reliably logs even to User recipients. Reverted to emailSimple/inline-HTML for this reason - it is the only mechanism proven to both send AND log for a User recipient in this org.

2026-09-14 fix: on rejection this flow previously only sent notifications - it never undid anything AF_FL_Quote_DiscountApproved/AF_FL_Quote_ApplySelfAuthorizedDiscount would have applied, and it never cleared the rejected request itself. Live-reported bug: TotalPrice stayed discounted after a rejection instead of reverting to the built/list price, and AF_DiscountAmount__c stayed populated with the rejected value. Fix mirrors AF_FL_Quote_DiscountApproved&apos;s own mechanism in reverse: loops every discountable QuoteLineItem on the Quote (not just the Vehicle line - same 2026-09-14 all-lines change as the Approved flow, since business feedback was the discount should apply to/revert from the whole Quote, not one line) and resets each line&apos;s native Discount (Percent) field to 0 - Salesforce recalculates each line&apos;s TotalPrice, and Quote.TotalPrice/Subtotal/GrandTotal, back to the undiscounted built price automatically, same recalc path Approved relies on to apply it. Get_All_Lines_Reject excludes AF_LineItemType__c = &quot;Trade-In Deduction&quot; and &quot;Discount Adjustment&quot; for the same reason as the Approved flow&apos;s Get_All_Lines - these are adjustment lines, not priced items, and touching a Trade-In Deduction line re-triggers its own unrelated AF_VR_QLI_TradeInDeductionGate validation (requires an Approved+Accepted linked Trade-In), confirmed live to fail the whole Rejected transaction otherwise. Also clears Quote.AF_DiscountAmount__c to null so the rejected amount doesn&apos;t linger on the record (AF_DiscountPercent__c is a formula off AF_DiscountAmount__c/Subtotal so it clears itself). Both of Quote&apos;s own discount validation rules (AF_VR_Quote_DiscountNotNegative, AF_VR_Quote_DiscountNotExceedSubtotal) are null-safe and do not block this. If the Quote has no discountable lines, the update collection stays empty and the line-reset update silently no-ops.</description>
